duduclaw-ai-runtimes — licence record for the vendored payload
==============================================================

This package redistributes third-party software it did not write. The
licences below were read off each component's own published metadata on
2026-09-05 (npm registry `license` field, PyPI classifier, or the upstream
repository's LICENSE file), not inferred from the project's reputation.
Two of the vendor binaries ship no licence file at all; they are recorded as
proprietary rather than guessed at.

The full texts, as shipped by each upstream, are installed on the image at
/opt/duduclaw/runtimes/LICENSES/ (the generator copies each npm package's
own LICENSE/LICENSE.md out of its tree, and fetches OpenCode's from its
tag). /opt/duduclaw/runtimes/MANIFEST.txt carries the exact version, source
URL and sha256 of every component, plus a `skipped:` line for anything not
present.

