Transitive npm and PyPI dependencies carry their own licences (overwhelm-
ingly MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD / ISC); the resolved set is recorded in
/opt/duduclaw/runtimes/package-lock.json and in the .dist-info directories
under /opt/duduclaw/runtimes/python.

Redistribution consequence, stated plainly: an image built with this
package is not freely redistributable on the strength of its open-source
components alone. The four proprietary entries above are subject
to their vendors' own terms, which is why this recipe sets
LICENSE_FLAGS = "duduclaw-ai-runtimes-vendor-terms" — any distro that wants
this payload has to accept those terms explicitly in its own configuration
rather than inherit them silently.
